{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ve been reviewing why you came in. You’ve been having nausea and vomiting, and your blood sugar was very high in the ER—432. We also saw signs of diabetic ketoacidosis. How have you been feeling since you got here?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still nauseous, honestly. I’ve been trying not to throw up, but it’s hard. I’ve been so stressed lately—getting ready to start the insulin pump. I think that’s making everything worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Stress can definitely trigger your gastroparesis and affect your blood sugar. We’ve started you on IV fluids and insulin to correct the DKA. Your anion gap was high at 24, but it’s already improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the DKA is getting better? I was scared when they said that in the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s resolving. Your latest labs show your bicarbonate is up to 24 and your anion gap is now 19—much better. We’ll keep the IV insulin running for a bit longer, then switch back to your usual injections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. But the nausea… it’s still there. I took Zofran at home, but it didn’t help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve added several anti-nausea meds: IV Zofran, Compazine, and we’re continuing your home Reglan. We also gave you Ativan in the ER, which helps with both nausea and anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do take Ativan at home, but clonazepam usually works better for me. Can I take that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re avoiding clonazepam this admission. We’ll use lorazepam instead, which is similar, and it’s on your discharge plan. We want to keep things consistent with what’s safest for you long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I guess that’s fine. I just want to feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re working on it. Your heart rate is still high—around 115. That’s common with dehydration and DKA, but it’s been persistent in past admissions too. We’ve checked for thyroid issues and infections before, and nothing’s shown up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, it’s always high when I’m in the hospital. I think it’s from the anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2199-07-19 05:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s very possible. Your EKG shows sinus tachycardia, which fits. No signs of heart strain. We’ll keep monitoring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2199-07-19 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I just reviewed your overnight labs. Your glucose is down to 231, and your kidney function is improving—creatinine is now 0.7. You’re definitely on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2199-07-19 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I haven’t thrown up since last night. I think I’m starting to feel a little better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2199-07-19 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’re going to try advancing your diet to clear liquids later today, if you’re up for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2199-07-19 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. But sometimes even water makes me feel worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2199-07-19 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll go slow. And we’ll keep the IV fluids running for now. Your team also noted that in past admissions, there were times when vomiting was self-induced. Is that something you’ve thought about?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2199-07-19 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I… I do sometimes make myself throw up when the nausea gets overwhelming. But only when I feel like I have to. It’s not that I’m faking it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2199-07-19 10:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I believe you. This pattern—severe nausea, vomiting, frequent admissions—has been seen in conditions like rumination syndrome or cyclic vomiting, which can be linked to anxiety. You’re not alone in this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2199-07-19 10:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My husband and I talked about it. We both think the stress of the pump transition is setting it off again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2199-07-19 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a really important insight. Managing stress could help prevent future episodes. We’d like to connect you with a psychologist you trust. Would you be open to that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2199-07-19 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to see the hospital psychiatrist, but I can find someone in my town. I just need to feel in control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2199-07-19 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely fair. We’ll support whatever therapist you choose. The goal is to help you manage these episodes before they lead to another hospital stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2199-07-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You slept well, I hear. You had a soft diet last night and kept it down. That’s a big step forward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2199-07-20 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I had applesauce and toast. Felt okay. Nausea is much better today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2199-07-20 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Your labs this morning are stable. No ketones, normal electrolytes. We’re going to stop the IV fluids and switch your insulin back to your home regimen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2199-07-20 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m going home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2199-07-20 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We want to make sure you’re consistently tolerating food and that your blood sugar stays in range. We’ll check again tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2199-07-20 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I really don’t want to be readmitted again. It’s exhausting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2199-07-20 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And we want to help you avoid that. That’s why managing stress and having a mental health plan is so important. You’ve already made progress by recognizing the pattern."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2199-07-20 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. You had lunch and kept it down. That’s three meals in a row—great job."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2199-07-20 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’m feeling more like myself. I haven’t taken any extra Ativan today, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2199-07-20 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a sign your anxiety is better controlled. We’ll send you home with ondansetron and lorazepam for breakthrough nausea, but the goal is to use them sparingly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2199-07-20 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my clonazepam? I usually take it twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2199-07-20 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching you to lorazepam as needed. It’s shorter-acting and safer in the long run. You can discuss restarting clonazepam with your doctor at follow-up, but for now, we’re keeping it simple."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news. Your labs are stable, you’ve tolerated a soft diet, and you haven’t vomited in over 24 hours. We’re clearing you for discharge today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What do I need to do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your home meds except clonazepam. Take the new ondansetron and lorazepam only if nausea returns. Follow up with your endocrinologist, and please make that therapist appointment. Stress management is key."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve already thought about who I want to see. I don’t want this to keep happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best step you can take. You’re strong, and you’re not alone in this. We’re here to support you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I really appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. The nurse will go over your discharge instructions and medications. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll have your husband come up when you’re ready. Get some rest and take it easy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if anything changes—especially blood sugar or nausea that won’t go away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve learned my limits."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s half the battle. Keep listening to your body."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m going to take it one day at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best way. You’ve done really well this admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I feel like I understand my body better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s huge. Knowledge is power, especially with chronic conditions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m going to start that journal I’ve been putting off—track my stress, food, blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s an excellent idea. It could help you and your doctors see patterns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to take control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you’re on your way. We’re proud of you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. That means a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve earned it. Now go home and rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2199-07-21 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Take care, Dr. Lee."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2199-07-19 04:48:00",
    "admission_end": "2199-07-21 17:10:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis, and anxiety was admitted for nausea, vomiting, and diabetic ketoacidosis with a blood glucose of 432 and an elevated anion gap. She was treated with IV fluids and insulin, which resolved her DKA. Persistent nausea was managed with antiemetics, and her tachycardia improved. Throughout the stay, she acknowledged that stress related to transitioning to an insulin pump contributed to her symptoms, and she recognized a pattern of self-induced vomiting during episodes. With support from her husband and medical team, she agreed to seek outpatient psychological care. By discharge, she was tolerating a soft diet, had no vomiting, and was stable. She was discharged home with medication adjustments and a plan for follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Personal history of peptic ulcer disease"
    ]
  }
}
